ProgramInterface Module Documentation
1. Introduction
The ProgramInterface module provides a user interface layer for a GW-BASIC-style interpreter. It supports live command-line editing, special key handling (e.g., function keys), and console rendering for an interactive text-based environment. This module ensures users can type, edit, and execute BASIC-like commands efficiently via keyboard input.

2. Dependencies
The module depends on the following components:
SystemInterface: Provides platform-independent I/O (input from keyboard, output to screen).
ScreenRenderer: Handles cursor movement and buffer redraws.
SpecialKeyHandler: Maps function keys (F1–F10) to command shortcuts like RUN, LIST, etc.
check_SKey structure: Encapsulates both normal and special key input.

3. Class Descriptions
*CommandLineEditor
Handles line-based text input from the user, including editing (insertion, deletion), cursor navigation, and interpretation of special keys like ENTER, ESC, arrows.

*SpecialKeyHandler
Captures function key (F1–F10) input and maps them to predefined commands (e.g., RUN, LIST). Injects the mapped command into the input buffer.

 *ScreenRenderer
Provides methods to visually render the input buffer and control the cursor's on-screen position for a DOS-style interface.

